FEX on Android: the guest's /tmp is always the RootFS's tmp.

Android 15 and later have a host /tmp the app cannot write, where host-first calls such as Wine's
server mkdir("/tmp/.wine-<uid>") fail with EACCES. FileManager replaces a leading "/tmp" with the
RootFS's tmp as a host path (FileManager::RootFSTmp) before anything else in Open, Openat, Stat,
Lstat, Access, FAccessat, FAccessat2, Readlink, Readlinkat, Chmod, Statx, Mknod, Mkdirat, Unlinkat,
Chdir, Statfs, NewFSStatAt and NewFSStatAt64, on every Android version. Other calls on /tmp
(absolute AF_UNIX paths, xattrs, rename, link, symlink, chown, utimensat, truncate, creat, inotify)
still go to the host. Only the exact component "/tmp" is matched.

